    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay so it was like... short-short (gap) long-short-short (gap) long. but the long one isn't just a pause, it feels like it's carrying a different weight. it's like it's \"speaking\" something. the intervals are roughly 0.5s, then a 1.2s gap, then 0.8s. when the server load went up, the 1.2s gap tightened to 0.9s. does that timing actually correlate to anything specific in a packet stream? it feels too deliberate to be just hardware interference.",
